<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Cleveland — Every Must-See, Ranked (Thu–Sun)</name>
<description>34 tier-1 stops. Import into Google My Maps: Create a new map &gt; Import.</description>
<Folder><name>Thursday · Suburbs, Metroparks &amp; Cuyahoga Valley</name><description>Thursday, because Holden closes Mondays and Tita Flora's closes Mondays. Everything else outdoors is open daily. Long driving day — start early.</description>
<Placemark><name>Holden Arboretum &amp; Stebbins Gulch</name><description>9:30 AM

Must-see · 1 source. Stebbins Gulch is guided-access only and must be booked ahead. Closed Mondays.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.3012572,41.6114292,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Squire's Castle</name><description>12:30 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Roofless stone gatehouse, free, dawn to dusk, directly on the road south.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.4192778,41.5800222,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cuyahoga Valley NP — Boston Mill Visitor Center</name><description>2:30 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Start here for maps and rangers.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.5603244,41.262604,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Brandywine Falls</name><description>3:30 PM

Must-see · 2 sources. Boardwalk to a 65-foot fall. Stairs at both levels — not fully accessible.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.538565,41.2769085,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Virginia Kendall Ledges Overlook</name><description>5:30 PM

Must-see · 2 sources. Best sunset in the national park. Arrive 45 min before sunset.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.5123348,41.2203118,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tita Flora's</name><description>7:30 PM

Must-eat · Filipino. Highest diner-rated Asian restaurant in the region. Closed Monday.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6400545,41.3851892,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Friday · University Circle &amp; the East Side</name><description>Friday, and not negotiable — the Dittrick opens Friday and Saturday only, and the art museum runs until 9pm on Fridays.</description>
<Placemark><name>Percy Skuy Collection, Dittrick Medical History Center</name><description>10:30 AM

Must-see · 2 sources. THE CONSTRAINT THAT SETS THE TRIP: Friday 10:30–4 and Saturday 12–4 only. Free.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.608414,41.5059193,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lucy, Cleveland Museum of Natural History</name><description>12:00 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Plus Balto and the Apollo 12 moon rock. Closed Mondays.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6130674,41.5114773,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Superior Phở</name><description>1:30 PM

Must-eat · TOP-SCORING FOOD, 3 sources. Enter through Golden Plaza, free parking. Closed Monday.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6696709,41.5103169,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wade Memorial Chapel</name><description>2:45 PM

Must-see · 1 source. THE BEST THING NOBODY TELLS YOU ABOUT: a Tiffany interior by an all-female workshop. Daily 10–4, free.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.5946413,41.5136209,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Haserot Angel</name><description>3:20 PM

Must-see · HIGHEST-SOURCED PLACE IN THE GUIDE, 3 sources. Section 9, Lot 14. Nearest landmark: Hanna Mausoleum.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.590375,41.513022,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lake View Cemetery — Garfield Memorial &amp; grounds</name><description>3:50 PM

Must-see · 2 sources. Climb the Garfield tower. Gates close 7:30pm Apr–Oct.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.5988944,41.51398,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cleveland Museum of Art &amp; The Thinker</name><description>4:50 PM

Must-see · 2 entries. Free, open to 9pm Fridays. The Rodin was bombed in 1970 and never restored.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6119723,41.5079261,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Presti's Bakery</name><description>7:30 PM

Must-eat · desserts. Century-old Little Italy bakery. Take a number or get cut in line.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.598356,41.50885,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Quintana's Speakeasy</name><description>8:45 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Buzzer at the barbershop's back door, then pull the right book. Closed Sun &amp; Mon.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.5563368,41.4998009,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Saturday · Downtown &amp; The Flats</name><description>Saturday, because the chess collection closes Sundays and the Terminal Tower deck opens weekends only. All ten downtown must-sees, ending under the chandelier after dark.</description>
<Placemark><name>Soldiers' &amp; Sailors' Monument</name><description>10:00 AM

Must-see · 1 source. Free museum. Ask whether the tunnels below are open — roughly one day a year.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6929283,41.4995228,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Chess Collection — Cleveland Public Library MAIN Library</name><description>10:45 AM

Must-see · 2 sources. 325 Superior Ave NE, third floor — NOT the address News 5 prints. Closed Sundays. Bring photo ID.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6916133,41.501113,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Arcade (Old Arcade)</name><description>11:45 AM

Must-see · 2 sources. 1890, America's first indoor shopping centre.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6902444,41.4999444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Heinen's Downtown</name><description>12:20 PM

Must-see · 1 source. A grocery inside a bank rotunda. Eat lunch on the balcony.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6861122,41.5000366,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Terminal Tower Observation Deck</name><description>1:20 PM

Must-see · 2 sources. Weekends only 12–4, tickets MUST be booked online. Ride to 32, transfer to 42.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6939263,41.4983959,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hope Memorial Bridge &amp; the Guardians of Traffic</name><description>2:30 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Eight art deco giants, 43 feet each. Walk it — pedestrian ways both sides.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6935635,41.4893486,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Steamship William G. Mather</name><description>3:30 PM

Must-see · 1 source. 618-foot freighter, open stem to stern. Closed Monday, seasonal.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6980733,41.5092703,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Free Stamp</name><description>4:20 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Rejected by the corporation that commissioned it. Two minutes, always open.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6924552,41.5054252,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rock &amp; Roll Hall of Fame</name><description>4:45 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Open to 8pm Saturdays. Buy ahead. Three hours minimum.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6953685,41.5085414,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wonton Gourmet &amp; BBQ</name><description>8:00 PM

Must-eat · Cantonese, 2 sources. Roast duck and char siu in the window. Open to 9:15pm. Closed Tuesday.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6662247,41.5088376,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>GE Chandelier, Playhouse Square</name><description>9:00 PM

Must-see · 2 sources. Largest outdoor chandelier in North America. Free, lit nightly. Go after dark.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6817691,41.5009131,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Sunday · West Side, Ohio City &amp; Tremont</name><description>Sunday, set by the market (10–4) and Buckland (12–4). Ends with sunset on the lake. Two west-side must-sees cannot fit — see README.</description>
<Placemark><name>West Side Market</name><description>10:00 AM

Must-see · HIGHEST-SOURCED PLACE IN THE GUIDE, 3 sources. Sunday 10–4. Bring cash. Park at the back.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7028394,41.4847078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mitchell's Ice Cream, Ohio City</name><description>11:30 AM

Must-eat · desserts. Made on site in a restored 1920s cinema. Two minutes from the market.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7044813,41.4858111,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Franklin Castle</name><description>12:15 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Interior is Tuesday-evening tours only — today is an exterior visit.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7165436,41.485723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>A Christmas Story House &amp; Museum</name><description>1:15 PM

Must-see · 2 sources. Tours every 30 min. Budget two hours, not one.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6874036,41.4687304,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Buckland Museum of Witchcraft &amp; Magick</name><description>3:00 PM

Must-see · 2 sources. Sunday 12–4 only. Gardner's artifacts and a demon in a box.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6998196,41.43805,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Barroco Arepa Bar</name><description>4:30 PM

Must-eat · Latin American, 2 sources. Colombian-Venezuelan. Waits get long and do not shorten.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7783683,41.477094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sweet Moses Soda Fountain</name><description>6:00 PM

Must-eat · desserts. A 1920s soda fountain rebuilt from scratch. Order the root beer float.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7319031,41.4838234,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Solstice Steps, Lakewood Park</name><description>7:45 PM

Must-see · 1 source. Best sunset in the region. Arrive 30 min early for a lower terrace.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.797965,41.4972086,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
</Document></kml>